OL,4,G1930FRadio 3 in Concert
OL,5,     GCellist Nicolas Altstaedt and
OL,6,     Gpianist Denes Varjon join The
OL,7,     GHalle for Kurtag's Double
OL,8,     GConcerto, before Thomas Ades
OL,9,     Gconducts his own work Lieux
OL,10,     Gretrouves and Debussy's vivid
OL,11,     GImages.
OL,12,G2145FThe Essay: The Death and Life of
OL,13,     FChristopher Marlowe
OL,14,     GJerry Brotton explores how, after
OL,15,     Ghe wrote what was to be his last
OL,16,     Gplay, The Massacre at Paris, Kit
OL,17,     GMarlowe found himself becoming
OL,18,     Gthe story.
